    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138-a2">

                <pb facs="0216" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg142"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 463.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pontifical Zouaves, Battalion
                                Headquarters,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Velletri,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 7, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">General</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Zouave John Watson has been arrested at Veroli, and will be taken, to-morrow
                    morning, under good escort, to Rome. While he was searched for at Trisulti,
                    which was his garrison, he was arrested by Captain De Lambilly, at Veroli, where
                    he was on leave. I have the honor also to inform your excellency that his name
                    is not Waston but Watson.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, general, your excellency’s very humble and obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lieutenant Colonel</hi>
                    ALLET.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">General,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of War, Rome.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
